1
00:00:08,551 --> 00:00:09,427
You said

2
00:00:10,052 --> 00:00:12,430
you'd hunt the ones you had to...

3
00:00:13,472 --> 00:00:15,891
and protect those of your choice.

4
00:00:18,978 --> 00:00:20,771
Didn't you?

5
00:00:21,981 --> 00:00:25,276
You're too naive to be a hunter.

6
00:00:27,778 --> 00:00:28,946
Shit!

7
00:00:30,448 --> 00:00:31,615
Nozomi!

8
00:00:32,783 --> 00:00:33,993
We're doomed!

9
00:00:42,710 --> 00:00:44,837
You messed up my space.

10
00:00:58,684 --> 00:01:01,312
I'm not sure if you get this.

11
00:01:02,062 --> 00:01:06,442
The Subject you let go
will go on to eat someone.

12
00:01:07,943 --> 00:01:10,112
It'll be your fault.

13
00:01:15,493 --> 00:01:20,122
Quit, if you can only kill the
monstrous ones.

14
00:01:21,499 --> 00:01:25,377
You'll just be a burden for
your teammates.

15
00:01:30,716 --> 00:01:33,302
Takayama...that's your name, right?

16
00:01:33,427 --> 00:01:37,348
How did you know about the bug?

17
00:01:37,515 --> 00:01:40,226
Are you tapping our radio?

18
00:01:40,851 --> 00:01:43,062
Maybe.

19
00:01:43,187 --> 00:01:44,730
Are you?

20
00:01:45,648 --> 00:01:50,236
No, I'm monitoring the police radio.

21
00:01:50,903 --> 00:01:55,908
How did you conclude a Subject
was behind this?

22
00:01:56,075 --> 00:02:00,871
Subjects don't waste meat by
letting it rot.

23
00:02:01,705 --> 00:02:02,540
A hunch.

24
00:02:02,748 --> 00:02:05,167
Right, a hunch.

25
00:02:06,335 --> 00:02:08,504
I guess so.

26
00:02:08,754 --> 00:02:13,467
That's the 2nd body to be found
hanging in the area.

27
00:02:16,178 --> 00:02:17,846
You didn't know?

28
00:02:19,390 --> 00:02:21,392
3 years ago.

29
00:02:22,726 --> 00:02:26,272
So a Subject didn't do this.

30
00:02:28,274 --> 00:02:29,233
A hunch...

31
00:02:30,568 --> 00:02:32,027
Sure, a hunch.

32
00:02:34,905 --> 00:02:39,535
Is he saying that this was
just a homicide?

33
00:02:40,369 --> 00:02:41,787
Maybe!

34
00:02:42,288 --> 00:02:45,749
Leave it to Nozomi and Mamoru.
We'll get the bug.

35
00:02:45,874 --> 00:02:48,919
As he said, the Subject
will attack again!

36
00:02:49,086 --> 00:02:52,923
I'm sorry. If I hadn't let him go...

37
00:02:53,340 --> 00:02:59,013
It happens. It's something
you never get used to.

38
00:03:00,681 --> 00:03:05,561
Get used to the fact that some
things you never get used to.

39
00:03:08,647 --> 00:03:09,898
Yes, sir.

40
00:03:25,331 --> 00:03:29,293
<i>Research here. We picked up a signal</i>
<i>for a split second.</i>

41
00:03:29,460 --> 00:03:30,502
Go!

42
00:03:39,970 --> 00:03:44,308
<i>Jin wants to know what</i>
<i>the Exterminators are doing.</i>

43
00:03:44,933 --> 00:03:47,478
<i>Easier said than done.</i>

44
00:03:48,687 --> 00:03:51,774
<i>I can't use the same old technique...</i>

45
00:04:06,622 --> 00:04:09,833
Hey! What are you after?

46
00:04:10,292 --> 00:04:15,130
Sorry, I'm just here to see Haruka...

47
00:04:15,673 --> 00:04:18,717
I mean, Haruka Mizusawa.

48
00:04:21,470 --> 00:04:26,225
Oh, is Haruka your friend?

49
00:04:26,725 --> 00:04:28,268
You know him?

50
00:04:33,565 --> 00:04:37,861
He's somewhere around.
This area is too vast!

51
00:04:39,363 --> 00:04:42,074
Can you sense anything, Haruka?

52
00:04:43,534 --> 00:04:46,745
Yes but I can't pinpoint it.

53
00:04:48,706 --> 00:04:52,668
We better not depend on that.
Let's split up.

54
00:04:52,751 --> 00:04:57,673
If you spot the Subject,
call the others.

55
00:04:58,424 --> 00:05:02,428
Haruka, you can fight him
if you're up to it.

56
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:04,012
OK.

57
00:05:04,888 --> 00:05:06,890
If you're up to it.

58
00:05:08,183 --> 00:05:09,518
Yes.

59
00:05:34,918 --> 00:05:36,879
I'll check on them...

60
00:05:40,758 --> 00:05:41,967
You bastard!

61
00:05:45,763 --> 00:05:47,806
Is he a bug, Mamoru?

62
00:05:48,223 --> 00:05:49,308
A human!

63
00:05:49,433 --> 00:05:50,601
What?

64
00:05:52,770 --> 00:05:53,645
You...!

65
00:05:54,229 --> 00:05:55,439
Who are you?

66
00:05:57,900 --> 00:05:59,443
A human...

67
00:06:04,656 --> 00:06:05,699
I'll get you.

68
00:06:08,702 --> 00:06:09,369
Oops!

69
00:06:10,829 --> 00:06:11,622
Nozomi.

70
00:06:16,668 --> 00:06:17,586
Nozomi!

71
00:06:17,711 --> 00:06:18,670
No.

72
00:06:19,421 --> 00:06:20,589
Don't.

73
00:06:21,924 --> 00:06:22,966
Why not?

74
00:06:24,218 --> 00:06:25,761
It's a man.

75
00:06:29,014 --> 00:06:31,892
Get out of here, Mamoru.

76
00:06:33,685 --> 00:06:34,937
Nozomi!

77
00:06:42,069 --> 00:06:46,114
Freeze...Monster.

78
00:07:14,852 --> 00:07:16,019
Any birds?

79
00:07:18,939 --> 00:07:20,607
- No.
- Oh...

80
00:07:21,733 --> 00:07:23,360
How nice!

81
00:07:24,194 --> 00:07:27,823
Hello, excuse me!

82
00:07:27,948 --> 00:07:34,037
This area is potentially hazardous
so please evacuate.

83
00:07:34,162 --> 00:07:34,872
What's he?

84
00:07:34,997 --> 00:07:36,039
Cosplay?

85
00:07:36,206 --> 00:07:37,875
Weird.

86
00:07:40,752 --> 00:07:44,506
Go on, watch your step.

87
00:07:45,924 --> 00:07:47,551
I'm weird...?

88
00:07:48,468 --> 00:07:51,638
That's one of the negatives
of this job.

89
00:08:24,254 --> 00:08:25,714
Fuku. Kazuya.

90
00:08:36,433 --> 00:08:37,851
No...

91
00:08:41,104 --> 00:08:42,773
Please don't!

92
00:08:58,497 --> 00:09:02,334
You're an Amazon too?

93
00:09:06,421 --> 00:09:10,384
Oh, it was you I fought...

94
00:09:15,931 --> 00:09:17,099
Did you

95
00:09:18,809 --> 00:09:20,102
ever eat...

96
00:09:21,395 --> 00:09:22,396
human meat?

97
00:09:27,609 --> 00:09:31,446
I had an urge...

98
00:09:33,740 --> 00:09:35,409
For the first time...

99
00:09:36,493 --> 00:09:40,163
I went into the junkyard
out of curiosity.

100
00:09:41,873 --> 00:09:42,708
And

101
00:09:44,543 --> 00:09:45,836
when I found it...!

102
00:09:48,255 --> 00:09:50,298
I couldn't help it.

103
00:09:51,216 --> 00:09:52,259
But...

104
00:09:53,427 --> 00:09:58,348
It was rotting so it wasn't edible.

105
00:10:00,934 --> 00:10:03,687
Who killed her then?

106
00:10:36,136 --> 00:10:40,807
What have you done to Mamoru?

107
00:10:43,643 --> 00:10:47,314
I'm just getting a workout.

108
00:10:47,981 --> 00:10:54,488
Since I was a kid, I loved hitting
things till they broke.

109
00:10:54,780 --> 00:10:56,823
It made me feel alive.

110
00:11:01,828 --> 00:11:03,997
It's very satisfying.

111
00:11:04,539 --> 00:11:06,124
Like this!

112
00:11:06,333 --> 00:11:07,584
Stop it!

113
00:11:08,585 --> 00:11:13,632
Mamoru, you can break those chains.

114
00:11:14,883 --> 00:11:15,717
Do it!

115
00:11:16,009 --> 00:11:18,095
But you'd be...

116
00:11:23,350 --> 00:11:26,520
Yes, you'd be beaten.

117
00:11:41,326 --> 00:11:42,661
Nozomi!

118
00:11:43,829 --> 00:11:45,997
Just go, Mamoru!

119
00:11:47,624 --> 00:11:50,544
I can't! Stop hitting her!

120
00:11:56,049 --> 00:11:59,219
I don't know what to make
of the creature.

121
00:12:00,011 --> 00:12:03,849
But I know you're the ones
invading my space.

122
00:12:04,599 --> 00:12:07,185
I'll exterminate you, Vermin.

123
00:12:09,980 --> 00:12:12,732
Nozomi! Stop hitting her!

124
00:12:25,328 --> 00:12:29,040
The junkyard owner is a murderer!

125
00:12:30,041 --> 00:12:31,209
I guess so.

126
00:12:32,586 --> 00:12:37,883
But I don't care what he does.

127
00:12:40,844 --> 00:12:45,390
Since then I've had this craving!

128
00:12:47,392 --> 00:12:51,438
I'm starving...!

129
00:12:55,901 --> 00:12:58,612
You don't have to eat humans.

130
00:12:59,821 --> 00:13:01,656
Some Amazons don't.

131
00:13:01,781 --> 00:13:03,283
No!

132
00:13:12,167 --> 00:13:14,044
It's in our...

133
00:13:18,131 --> 00:13:19,591
nature!

134
00:13:25,096 --> 00:13:25,972
Amazon!

135
00:13:28,975 --> 00:13:30,393
Are you OK?

136
00:13:31,728 --> 00:13:35,565
So you know Haruka is an Amazon.

137
00:13:36,441 --> 00:13:39,778
And you want to take him home?

138
00:13:40,987 --> 00:13:45,408
It's not his true nature
to fight like that.

139
00:13:47,452 --> 00:13:51,998
He's gentle and
he loves tropical fish.

140
00:13:52,832 --> 00:13:54,334
He's nice to me too.

141
00:13:54,834 --> 00:13:56,836
<i>Hi Mizuki.</i>

142
00:13:57,504 --> 00:14:02,968
Ever since Mom adopted him
I've loved being with him.

143
00:14:04,135 --> 00:14:09,266
My home was cold
until he came along.

144
00:14:11,184 --> 00:14:15,397
Haruka was peaceful
when he was in his room.

145
00:14:16,898 --> 00:14:20,777
<i>I guess this room is my aquarium.</i>

146
00:14:22,737 --> 00:14:26,658
I don't know why he had to
become so hideous

147
00:14:27,242 --> 00:14:29,369
and fight so desperately.

148
00:14:35,458 --> 00:14:37,335
It's terrible!

149
00:14:38,003 --> 00:14:41,339
So I decided that
I have to save him.

150
00:14:42,007 --> 00:14:43,550
But you see...

151
00:14:45,218 --> 00:14:47,554
it's not your business.

152
00:14:50,348 --> 00:14:55,061
Sorry...but it was me
who gave him the Amazon belt.

153
00:14:56,396 --> 00:14:57,480
Why?

154
00:15:02,986 --> 00:15:04,321
So he'd survive.

155
00:15:07,115 --> 00:15:08,616
Survive...?

156
00:15:37,020 --> 00:15:38,688
<i>The Subject you let go</i>

157
00:15:39,689 --> 00:15:44,569
<i>will eat someone</i>
<i>and it'll be your fault.</i>

158
00:16:25,068 --> 00:16:27,362
He's matured!

159
00:16:32,283 --> 00:16:35,912
The victim appears to be alive.
Help him.

160
00:16:38,039 --> 00:16:42,293
Haruka chose to leave his cage
and start living.

161
00:16:47,048 --> 00:16:49,259
It's not easy on him but

162
00:16:50,176 --> 00:16:53,805
it's better than being in a cage.

163
00:16:53,972 --> 00:16:56,141
It's not a cage!

164
00:16:56,641 --> 00:17:00,937
This time he'd be free to come and go.

165
00:17:01,020 --> 00:17:03,815
Do you think he'd be free
that way?

166
00:17:15,952 --> 00:17:20,415
What does everyone want from Haruka...?

167
00:17:23,710 --> 00:17:26,713
Haruka isn't a hunter!

168
00:17:29,090 --> 00:17:30,425
Right.

169
00:18:11,549 --> 00:18:14,469
Get him! He's our meal ticket!

170
00:18:16,638 --> 00:18:18,181
Come on, Haruka!

171
00:18:45,917 --> 00:18:49,128
OK, we'll rendezvous with
Nozomi and Mamoru.

172
00:19:06,688 --> 00:19:09,566
It's hard to kill a monster!

173
00:19:10,066 --> 00:19:14,946
This is the best!
I feel so alive.

174
00:19:19,576 --> 00:19:22,787
I'll get you, sucker...

175
00:19:24,414 --> 00:19:26,499
I'll get you.

176
00:19:33,298 --> 00:19:34,090
Haruka!

177
00:19:37,719 --> 00:19:39,137
Nozomi!

178
00:19:41,139 --> 00:19:42,015
Nozomi.

179
00:19:42,140 --> 00:19:44,434
Oh, she got it bad.

180
00:19:44,934 --> 00:19:45,643
Are you OK?

181
00:19:45,768 --> 00:19:47,604
Take this off!

182
00:19:52,066 --> 00:19:53,109
No...

183
00:19:54,110 --> 00:19:55,111
Don't...

184
00:20:04,912 --> 00:20:06,456
Bastard!

185
00:20:06,748 --> 00:20:07,665
You can't!

186
00:20:07,790 --> 00:20:09,167
Why not?

187
00:20:09,375 --> 00:20:10,710
He's a man.

188
00:20:11,044 --> 00:20:12,378
Yeah, but...

189
00:20:13,671 --> 00:20:14,797
Nozomi.

190
00:20:30,396 --> 00:20:33,650
You have a tendency to go berserk.

191
00:20:33,983 --> 00:20:35,234
Out of my way!

192
00:20:35,401 --> 00:20:37,528
Forget it.

193
00:20:38,029 --> 00:20:41,699
He's a murderer!

194
00:20:44,077 --> 00:20:45,912
So what?

195
00:20:48,915 --> 00:20:50,583
Get off me...

196
00:20:54,379 --> 00:20:56,381
Get off!

197
00:20:59,926 --> 00:21:01,302
Off!

198
00:21:02,428 --> 00:21:04,305
Get off!

199
00:21:07,183 --> 00:21:08,518
Alright.

200
00:21:17,068 --> 00:21:18,778
Hey, wait a minute...

201
00:21:19,904 --> 00:21:20,905
No...

202
00:21:39,757 --> 00:21:41,050
Why...?

203
00:21:42,301 --> 00:21:43,761
Listen.

204
00:21:44,721 --> 00:21:50,351
I draw a line between
Amazons and humans.

205
00:21:51,811 --> 00:21:53,271
Meaning

206
00:21:57,358 --> 00:22:02,029
I'll protect a human
no matter how horrible he is.

207
00:22:02,321 --> 00:22:04,157
That's all.

208
00:22:07,452 --> 00:22:08,828
But

209
00:22:11,247 --> 00:22:12,915
he is a...

210
00:22:18,087 --> 00:22:19,589
You...

211
00:22:20,798 --> 00:22:24,635
You said I exterminate Amazons
as I please.

212
00:22:28,306 --> 00:22:30,975
I could say that about you.

213
00:22:39,317 --> 00:22:46,115
You randomly choose who to kill
and who to protect.

214
00:22:48,201 --> 00:22:53,998
Without a code, you're inconsistent.

215
00:22:58,419 --> 00:22:59,879
We're out of here.

216
00:23:04,884 --> 00:23:07,970
Haruka, let's go.

217
00:23:09,305 --> 00:23:10,556
Are you OK?

218
00:23:11,682 --> 00:23:12,892
Nozomi?

219
00:23:16,813 --> 00:23:18,481
You bastard!

220
00:23:34,747 --> 00:23:37,333
Do we have a code?

221
00:23:38,417 --> 00:23:43,422
Yes. What we do is too tough
to do without one.

222
00:23:44,382 --> 00:23:49,428
That's why we only kill
those with a price tag.

223
00:23:50,388 --> 00:23:54,267
Money keeps us from being confused.

224
00:23:55,768 --> 00:24:00,439
Remember that
we aren't heroes.

225
00:24:09,907 --> 00:24:14,328
<i>But I wanted to...</i>

226
00:24:18,541 --> 00:24:22,879
No matter what you say
I want to bring Haruka home.

227
00:24:34,015 --> 00:24:35,474
It hurts...

228
00:24:35,725 --> 00:24:37,143
Are you OK?

229
00:24:41,814 --> 00:24:42,815
Here.

230
00:24:43,107 --> 00:24:46,485
You could've come sooner.

231
00:24:47,653 --> 00:24:49,155
You're welcome.

232
00:24:51,490 --> 00:24:54,785
That sounded like a <i>Thank you.</i>

233
00:24:54,952 --> 00:24:58,456
You're getting used to this, Master!

234
00:24:59,123 --> 00:25:01,125
I'm not <i>Master.</i>

235
00:25:01,792 --> 00:25:05,421
We're out of here.
Let's get drunk.

236
00:25:05,546 --> 00:25:08,132
Yes! Let's go!

237
00:25:17,850 --> 00:25:22,438
Thank you for your time, Chairman.

238
00:25:23,147 --> 00:25:24,941
Tachibana.

239
00:25:25,608 --> 00:25:30,279
Of course I always have time for you.

240
00:25:31,530 --> 00:25:37,787
You and your team have been
developing your project for years.

241
00:25:38,955 --> 00:25:42,792
But there's been no results.

242
00:25:44,043 --> 00:25:46,045
Pardon me.

243
00:25:46,545 --> 00:25:52,385
I didn't want to bother you
with the details.

244
00:25:53,052 --> 00:25:57,223
So you're telling me that
this is worth my time?

245
00:25:57,348 --> 00:26:03,896
Yes. The enhanced Amazon
with superior cells

246
00:26:04,230 --> 00:26:06,774
is almost complete.

247
00:26:07,024 --> 00:26:08,234
Almost?

248
00:26:09,318 --> 00:26:13,197
I dislike ambiguous reports.

249
00:26:13,322 --> 00:26:15,324
I understand.

250
00:26:15,825 --> 00:26:20,371
So here's the thing.
To reach completion

251
00:26:20,705 --> 00:26:25,501
I need your authority and help.

252
00:26:28,838 --> 00:26:31,048
The Amazon belt.

253
00:26:32,633 --> 00:26:37,763
If I can access the belt's data,
it'll soon be ready.

254
00:27:30,983 --> 00:27:32,985
Is it a bug meeting?

255
00:27:33,444 --> 00:27:36,113
Run if you want freedom!

256
00:27:36,238 --> 00:27:37,239
They're bugs!

257
00:27:37,406 --> 00:27:39,075
They haven't awakened.

258
00:27:39,241 --> 00:27:39,658
No!

259
00:27:39,867 --> 00:27:42,078
So you're the prototype?

260
00:27:42,203 --> 00:27:43,204
Amazon.
